<section id="execution"><h2>What actually ran</h2><div class="columns"><article class="card"><h3>B063R2 · actual owner return</h3><div id="execution-actual"></div></article><article class="card"><h3>B063R3 · prepared continuation</h3><p>The continuation retains recovered models, input-bound cache identities and the 6,320-context research queue. Production results must be established by its own worker, CPU, memory, fit and return ledgers.</p><p><strong>Recovery is not retraining.</strong> The 115 selected model chains have matching model bytes, reports, input proofs and training-membership hashes. Runtime reuse requires the relevant runtime and scientific input identities to match.</p><p>The broader ledger reports lower bounds of 245 target estimators, 48 calibrations and 24 residual fits. Exact overall totals remain unknown; these categories are not added to checkpoint counts.</p></article></div></section>
<section id="historical"><h2>Which models lead each completed season?</h2><p class="note">The same season, target and eligible game cohort are compared within each group. The panel includes all 12 retained recipes plus selected native candidates, with 13–14 candidates per target and season. It does not rank all 6,320 registered contexts or every native model. These are development-exposed historical research leaders; no automatic promotion follows.</p><p class="count" id="season-leader-count" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="season-leaders" class="scroll"></div><h3>Pooled 2024–25 and 2025–26 leaders</h3><p class="note">These 14 target-specific results compare the saved retained and native research panels. They are separate from the current-season leaderboard. A different model may lead each metric; no paired significance claim is made.</p><div id="pooled-leaders" class="scroll"></div></section>
<section id="candidates"><h2>Every saved candidate-season result</h2><p class="note">All 164 candidate-season rows are retained in this table and in the downloadable source. Accuracy uses the recorded tie convention. MAE and RMSE are points for margin and total models. Missing metrics remain blank.</p><p><a href="data/NCAA_B063R2_PUBLIC_SCIENTIFIC_TABLES.json" download>Download complete scientific tables (JSON)</a> · <button type="button" id="download-candidates">Download filtered candidates (CSV)</button></p><div class="pager"><p class="count" id="candidate-count" aria-live="polite"></p><button type="button" id="candidate-prev">Previous</button><button type="button" id="candidate-next">Next</button></div><div id="candidate-table" class="scroll"></div></section>
<section id="current"><h2>2026–27 · descriptive current-season replay</h2><p class="note"><strong>These are reconstructed saved predictions, not a record of original pregame issuance.</strong> The largest exact common cohorts contain 420 men's games and 403 women's games at the saved evidence cutoff. Full official-season coverage through today is not certified. Current outcomes do not select a frozen historical champion or confer promotion.</p><p class="count" id="current-count" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="current-leaders" class="scroll"></div><h3>B003 original frozen model · retained replay</h3><div id="b003-table" class="scroll"></div><h3>How difficult was this observed cohort?</h3><p class="note">An always-home direction baseline helps interpret the early-season accuracy. It has no fitted probability, so probability log loss and Brier are not invented for that baseline.</p><div id="home-baselines" class="scroll"></div></section>
<section id="markets"><h2>DraftKings, Kalshi and Polymarket</h2><p class="note">Each comparison requires the same event, outcome, horizon, settlement rule and eligible quote clock. Provider products remain distinct. Missing qualified pairs are missing evidence, not perfect model performance.</p><div id="provider-table" class="scroll"></div><h3>B003 vs Polymarket International · matched men's cohort</h3><p class="note">338 matched games in the saved reconstructed comparison. Model direction accuracy is slightly higher; the market has lower log loss and Brier. Three week blocks are insufficient for the configured interval, so no confidence interval or statistically established outperformance is claimed. This is not a comparison with Polymarket US.</p><div id="paired-market" class="scroll"></div></section>
<section id="originals"><h2>Original forecasts with later final scores</h2><p class="note">These are separate original-issue cohorts. Prediction values and issue clocks remain unchanged; later official outcomes live in a separate observation layer. Aggregate metrics use original full precision. The cohorts differ in models and eligibility and are not pooled into a single accuracy or ensemble.</p><div class="columns"><article class="card"><h3>Earlier selected roles</h3><p>30 games: four men and 26 women. Ninety original target forecasts, six preselected model/target groups. All selected games have later verified final observations.</p><p id="early-clock" class="subtle"></p><a href="data/B063_PUBLIC_EARLY_ORIGINAL_POSTISSUE_MONITORING.json" download>Download earlier-cohort monitoring</a></article><article class="card"><h3>Later native candidates</h3><p>Eight disjoint games: six men and two women. Forty-six original target forecasts, 11 candidate/component groups. Ensemble components remain separate forecasts.</p><p id="late-clock" class="subtle"></p><a href="data/B063_PUBLIC_LATE_ORIGINAL_POSTISSUE_MONITORING.json" download>Download later-cohort originals and results</a></article></div><h3>Earlier selected-role metrics</h3><div id="early-groups" class="scroll"></div><h3>Later candidate and component metrics</h3><div id="late-groups" class="scroll"></div><details><summary>Inspect all 46 later original forecast rows</summary><p class="note">Winner probability is for the home team; margin is home points minus away points; total combines both teams. Displayed prediction values are rounded. Error metrics were calculated from the exact original values. Original issuance precedes the recorded cutoff; actual points come from the later linked observation.</p><div id="late-rows" class="scroll"></div></details><details><summary>Official outcome sources for both original-issue cohorts</summary><div id="outcome-sources" class="scroll"></div></details><h3>Upcoming games and rolling forecasts</h3><p class="note">No new future forecast was issued in this continuation review. The preserved dashboard retains the earlier source-game census and original issues. A fresh owner run must refresh schedule truth, qualify inputs and issue new forecasts before they can be described as the latest upcoming predictions. Final rolling-native report completion remains pending.</p><p><a href="index.html#b063-game-section">Inspect all preserved completed and upcoming source-game records →</a></p></section>
<section id="promotion"><h2>What is good enough for promotion?</h2><div class="columns"><article class="card"><h3>Evidence first, by target</h3><p>Compare the candidate and incumbent on identical games, timestamps, information horizons and settlement definitions. Preserve 2024–25 and 2025–26 frozen evaluations, rolling-origin partitions, source vintages and original issue clocks.</p><p>The inherited historical research eligibility includes 500 common games, 100 per completed season, eight time clusters and at least 500 training rows across three seasons. These are research eligibility requirements, not an automatic production promotion rule.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>A measured improvement with guardrails</h3><p>Pre-register the primary target and metric, uncertainty method, multiplicity control, calibration/stability limits and rollback. Confirm improvement on the relevant held-out or prospective evidence without selecting models on the same current outcomes later called prospective.</p><p>There is no universal 80% accuracy or 0.4 log-loss pass mark. Winner accuracy, probability quality, margin errors and total errors answer different questions. Missing market comparisons and small early-season cohorts cannot establish production superiority.</p></article></div><details><summary>Evidence qualifications and source hashes</summary><ul id="scope-notes"></ul><div id="source-pins"></div></details></section>
